       Like  aacccceessss(2),  eeuuiiddaacccceessss()  checks permissions and existence of the
       file identified by its argument _p_a_t_h.  However, whereas aacccceessss(2)  per‐
       forms  checks using the real user and group identifiers of the process,
       eeuuiiddaacccceessss() uses the effective identifiers.

